{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the following double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-38467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/a85f82756c621bf88b95451f54343be863345278f361fd0f0dd82f5d01c0cb5b.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8243a8c60e4b8b4846d330a00a090d6f93f94f17323c1d0a88d486ba77745451.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{[\\frac{2}{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{2{y}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{2}[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-38467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfbc00a552f6d65c9754823e566f8471a6b54f63a954426a377fb76723543c6e"} {"question" "q-38467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-38467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}+1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-38467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x-2}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/0119869a8627edfaf9c16f905908d378b94c9566b0a6b7742c813c35f58d4699.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2x-2\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/3fe0d83ae8f99f443646be4e84687104edaeef58a83e68da7e832630f31efda7.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\frac{y+2}{2}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{y+2}{2}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{1-y}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x-2}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfbc00a552f6d65c9754823e566f8471a6b54f63a954426a377fb76723543c6e"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{(y+2)/2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{(y+2)/2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-82350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/9a539f69187276895f8f53e2107c1959fefd0aeb7126dcff049569bfc8bc49d3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y-2\\le x\\le 0}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y-2\\,⟹\\,y=x+2,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-y-2\\,⟹\\,y=-x-2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-2\\le y\\le x+2},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/ba9c9132c8efdb811e63bebc05e1f46bc8cbc54bcb8246072013a75d53bcb4df.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfbc00a552f6d65c9754823e566f8471a6b54f63a954426a377fb76723543c6e"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/926e4c717707d13fdb9562e149d2f41c3ab657b42fbae35c0953019ab93a06b6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le -y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8933233e8aca4a36ee90ffec69ca6e93d0523d3fa50c400d2cdea78f9ec80812.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=\\sqrt{-x-1}\\,$ and $\\,y=1.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,\\sqrt{-x-1}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le -x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfbc00a552f6d65c9754823e566f8471a6b54f63a954426a377fb76723543c6e"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8ed09966d887f66f36402df0047ba02444d92b8aa4c3cb744721bb4ad6278812.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 0}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=-1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-1\\le y\\le {x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/f707a71f68f2e030696029d9a919e16ae6afda18a1d60dc3f8113f03143243e7.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)[{\\int }_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\cdot y\\,{|}_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{3}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{4}+4(0))-(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-1)^{4}+4(-1))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfbc00a552f6d65c9754823e566f8471a6b54f63a954426a377fb76723543c6e"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3)"] ["math" "4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1}{4}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"} {"question" "q-132635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/state.json" "file_sha256" "09385854e105c7ec0e6eabe347335a068715e45caae3abb56fb2e917c7f1fa21"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2823 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
